  "number": 2131,
  "state": "closed",
  "locked": false,
  "title": "fix(formal-ai): run native CLIs against a Formal AI endpoint instead of the argv wrapper",
  "user": { "login": "konard", "id": 1431904, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard", "html_url": "https://github.com/konard", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false },
  "body": "## What this fixes\n\n`--model formal-ai` produced no work on a hello-world issue for every tool tried in the report — `claude`, `codex`, and `agent` (the last across 18 restarts). Three separate root causes, all in the same place: Hive Mind invoked each CLI **through the `formal-ai with <tool> …` argv wrapper**, and the wrapper rewrites the argv it is given.\n\n| Tool     | What actually happened                                                                                                                                                             |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `claude` | The caller's `-p <prompt>` never reached the CLI. A workspace-effect keyword anywhere in argv flipped the wrapper into a recovery path that consumed stdin and substituted its own prompt. |\n| `agent`  | The argv was reordered and `--interactive` was injected into a headless, piped invocation.                                                                                          |\n| `codex`  | `exec` was dropped, and `-c` overrides placed after `exec` discarded the ones placed before it — `model_provider` fell back to `openai` and the run 401'd against `api.openai.com`. |\n\nFixes #2130.\n\n## The fix\n\nStop going through the argv wrapper. Hive Mind now starts `formal-ai serve --agent-mode` once per run and points **the native CLI** at that endpoint through each tool's own configuration channel, so nothing can rewrite the argv, drop the prompt, or redirect the traffic:\n\n| Tool                 | Channel                                                                     |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `codex`              | `CODEX_HOME` with a generated `config.toml` (`model_provider` pinned)       |\n| `gemini`             | `GEMINI_CLI_SYSTEM_SETTINGS_PATH` with `security.auth.selectedType`         |\n| `qwen`               | `OPENAI_BASE_URL` + `OPENAI_API_KEY` + `OPENAI_MODEL`                        |\n| `claude`/`agent`/`opencode` | `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` / provider env, via the client registry           |\n\nEverything is materialised under `~/.cache/hive-mind/formal-ai/<tool>` (not `/tmp` — codex refuses PATH helpers under `/tmp`). The operator's `HOME`, git, `gh` and ssh configuration is never shadowed, and for `sh -lc` invocations the environment is re-exported inside the script so a stale `formal-ai with --global` block in `~/.profile` cannot override it.\n\nNew: `src/formal-ai-runtime.lib.mjs`, `src/codex.run-diagnostics.lib.mjs`, `src/quiet-probe.lib.mjs`.\n\n## Hive-Mind-side false positives, warnings and errors (R1)\n\nEvery one of these is evidenced by a line in the stored solver logs:\n\n- **False negative** — \"No working session summary available from AI tool output\" for a session that produced one. Agent 0.25.x nests assistant text under `part`, so `data.text` was always empty.\n- **False positive** — codex printed a `WARNING` on every run about a `last-message` file that a failed run is not expected to have written.\n- **False positive** — an expected `gh: Not Found (HTTP 404)` existence probe printed as an error.\n- **Error** — `gh auth setup-git` fails on a bind-mounted `~/.gitconfig` (`Device or resource busy`); Hive Mind continued with **no** credential helper. It now falls back to clone-local config.\n- **Wrong remedy** — \"Please run: codex login\" for a model that is not served by codex's own account.\n\n## Log noise, applied across the whole codebase (R10)\n\nRead-only probes mirrored their raw payloads into the log that `--attach-logs` uploads: a ~33 KB PR object once per watch iteration, up to 46 KB of comments per restart, and — worst — **`gh auth status --show-token` printing a live credential in clear text**. The `quietProbe`/`QUIET_PROBE` idiom is applied to all 20 affected modules, with a repo-wide static test guarding against regressions.\n\n## Debug output for the next iteration (R9)\n\nThe Formal AI wrapper version is now recorded in the solve log on both the success and failure paths, and the runtime logs its endpoint, protocol, config root and environment. Codex's run diagnostics were extracted into pure, unit-testable functions.\n\n## Upstream reports (R2)\n\nEight issues filed against `link-assistant/formal-ai`, each with a re-runnable reproduction committed under [`experiments/issue-2130`](experiments/issue-2130/):\n\n| Issue                                                       | Defect                                                                            |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| [#902](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/902) | codex `-c` overrides before `exec` discarded once any `-c` follows it            |\n| [#903](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/903) | argv construction defects across all six clients                                  |\n| [#904](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/904) | agent mode reduces a repo task to plan-and-`cat`                                  |\n| [#905](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/905) | success claimed for a turn in which every tool call failed                        |\n| [#906](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/906) | \"no synthesis route\" unless the prompt names a language                           |\n| [#907](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/907) | intent router answers the caller's framing — gemini's injected date line hijacks every run |\n| [#908](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/908) | verification verdict tracks output presence, not the exit code                    |\n| [#909](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/909) | `--global` writes a config both gemini and qwen refuse to start from               |\n\n**Negative result, recorded deliberately:** no `link-assistant/agent` filing is warranted. The 18 restarts were Hive Mind's own auto-restart-until-mergeable feature reacting to a run that produced nothing — `agent` 0.25.5 exits 0 in 4 s on closed piped stdin, with *and* without the injected `--interactive` ([`repro-agent-interactive-stdin.mjs`](experiments/issue-2130/repro-agent-interactive-stdin.mjs)). An earlier draft of the case study claimed otherwise; that claim is corrected here and [upstream in #903](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/903#issuecomment-5160227783).\n\n## Case study and data (R6, R7, R8)\n\n[`docs/case-studies/issue-2130`](docs/case-studies/issue-2130/) — timeline, the full requirement inventory (R1–R10) with status, per-tool root causes with quoted log lines, upstream defects with reproductions, a survey of existing components considered, and a solution-plan table. Supporting data:\n\n- `data/tool-logs/` — the 7 solver logs from all three runs (including all 18 agent restarts), sanitized\n- `data/runs/` — captured output of every experiment\n- `data/probes/` — verbatim Formal AI answers\n- `data/github/` — 30 API captures across 6 repositories\n\n## How to reproduce and verify\n\n```bash\n# Before: the prompt never arrives\nnode experiments/issue-2130/probe-stdin.mjs\n\n# After: every CLI reaches Formal AI and exits 0\nnode experiments/issue-2130/e2e-direct-endpoint.mjs claude agent codex qwen gemini opencode\n```\n\nAutomated coverage: `tests/test-issue-2130-formal-ai-runtime.mjs` (478 lines) and `tests/test-issue-2130-log-noise.mjs` (316 lines).\n\nEvery experiment script writes into a throwaway `HOME`, so `formal-ai with … --global` never touches the operator's real `~/.profile`.\n\n## Checks\n\n`npm test` (372 files), `npm run lint` and `npm run format:check` all pass locally.\n",
